# Host redirect rules. Netlify and Cloudflare Pages read this file verbatim;
# Vercel wants the same rules in vercel.json, and nginx/Apache in their own
# config. If the site is served somewhere that ignores this file, the two 301s
# below still need to exist there, or the old URLs 404.
#
# Existing files always win over these rules, so the prerendered
# /coworking/index.html is served directly and never falls through.

# The Eat & Work page is gone — the business has no restaurant. Both of its old
# URLs point at the workspace page that replaced it. 301, not 302: the move is
# permanent, and only a 301 passes on whatever ranking the old URLs held.
/eat-and-work    /coworking    301
/restaurant      /coworking    301

# The old /coworking path already resolves to the real page, so it needs no rule.

# SPA fallback, last. Any path with no prerendered file is handed index.html and
# React Router sorts it out client-side. Kept at 200 rather than a redirect so
# the URL the visitor typed survives.
/*               /index.html   200
